Cell["\<\
Unfortunately, we can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t construct the traditional Dirac \
matrices (interpreted as vectors in Cl(3,1) algebra)  using Kronecker product \
of matrices from Cl(3,1) decomposition. This is because traditional Dirac \
matrices have metric (1,-1,-1,-1), while Cl(3,1) metric has opposite  signs \
(1,1,1,-1). The closest set obtained in this way differ by some signs and has \
Cl(3,1) metric.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQAWIQnV+6VEYz/rVj+LlnyiD65TxHBxD9dCevE4iuVL6a
